{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>This month.</b> He showed him the moon in its renewal and said to him: When the moon renews itself, that shall be for you the head of the month (Mekhilta). And the verse does not depart from its plain sense — regarding the month of Nisan He said to him: This shall be the head for the order of counting the months, so that Iyyar is called second, Sivan third." "<b>This.</b> Moses found it difficult concerning the molad of the moon — at what measure does it appear and become fit for sanctification? And He showed him the moon in the sky with a finger and said to him: Like this — see and sanctify (ibid.). And how did He show it to him? For was He not spoken with only by day? As it says: ״וַיְהִי בְּיוֹם דִּבֶּר ה׳״ (Exodus 6), ״בְּיוֹם צַוֹּתוֹ״ (Leviticus 7), ״מִן הַיּוֹם אֲשֶׁר צִוָּה ה׳ וָהָלְאָה״ (Numbers 15)? Rather, close to sunset this pericah was said to him, and He showed it to him with darkness."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:32.339584393Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}